WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:07.842
"Was that Mrs.

2
00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:16.666
Jackson raced down the alley.

3
00:00:17.626 --> 00:00:18.827
Henry and Maggie followed.

4
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.968
The alley was between the Sweet Shop and another store.

5
00:00:22.969 --> 00:00:24.469
At the back was a small shed.

6
00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:30.052
Mrs. Sweet stood there facing Miss Bishop, who owned the jewelry store across the street.

7
00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:32.689
"Oh my, Laura!"

8
00:00:33.089 --> 00:00:35.031
Miss Bishop fanned her face with one hand.

9
00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:39.134
"You nearly gave me a heart attack sneaking up on me like that!"

10
00:00:39.154 --> 00:00:42.396
"I wasn't sneaking, Jane," Mrs.

11
00:00:42.456 --> 00:00:43.237
Sweet retorted.

12
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:46.099
"I was just walking to my shed.

13
00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.460
What were you doing back here anyway?

14
00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:51.302
Trying to get a peek at my float, hmm?"

15
00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:53.604
"Of course not!"

16
00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:56.746
Just then Miss Bishop noticed Henry and the others.

17
00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:58.788
"Oh, hello."

18
00:00:59.828 --> 00:01:01.009
"Is everything all right, ladies?"

19
00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:02.150
Jackson asked.

20
00:01:02.811 --> 00:01:03.511
"We heard a scream."

21
00:01:03.531 --> 00:01:05.393
"That was me."

22
00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:06.794
Miss Bishop smiled.

23
00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:09.096
"Mrs. Sweet startled me."

24
00:01:10.257 --> 00:01:12.399
Henry traded an amused look with Maggie.

25
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.483
They both knew that Miss Bishop was a very dramatic person.

26
00:01:16.503 --> 00:01:18.985
"I see," Jackson said.

27
00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:21.527
"Mrs. Sweet, can I talk to you?"

28
00:01:22.528 --> 00:01:23.229
"Of course."

29
00:01:23.989 --> 00:01:26.672
Mrs. Sweet shot Miss Bishop a suspicious look.

30
00:01:27.616 --> 00:01:29.657
"Just let me lock my shed first.

31
00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:33.939
I wouldn't want anyone wandering in and getting a look at my float."

32
00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:36.420
Miss Bishop rolled her eyes.

33
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.381
"Why would anyone want to do that?"

34
00:01:42.162 --> 00:01:43.943
Soon Miss Bishop returned to her shop.

35
00:01:44.963 --> 00:01:47.364
Henry, Maggie, Jackson, and Mrs.

36
00:01:47.404 --> 00:01:48.885
Sweet headed into the Sweet Shop.

37
00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:53.307
"I heard you had some trouble last night," Jackson said to Mrs.

38
00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:55.908
Sweet. He pulled out a notebook and pen.

39
00:01:56.692 --> 00:01:57.993
"Someone broke into your shed?"

40
00:01:58.013 --> 00:02:01.176
"Yes." Mrs.

41
00:02:01.216 --> 00:02:02.057
Sweet shook her head.

42
00:02:02.077 --> 00:02:04.139
"It was a terrible shock."

43
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.860
"What happened?"

44
00:02:06.121 --> 00:02:07.021
Maggie blurted out.

45
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:09.404
"Did someone sabotage your float?"

46
00:02:09.424 --> 00:02:11.405
"I'm not sure."

47
00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:13.067
Mrs. Sweet looked troubled.

48
00:02:13.087 --> 00:02:16.650
"I left the shed unlocked last night so Mr.

49
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.453
Newman could stop by on his way home from work.

50
00:02:20.413 --> 00:02:23.016
I needed him to fix the taillight on my tractor."

51
00:02:24.268 --> 00:02:26.630
"Mr. Newman from the auto repair shop?"

52
00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.531
Henry asked.

53
00:02:27.551 --> 00:02:30.433
"Yes, that's right," Mrs.

54
00:02:30.493 --> 00:02:31.114
Sweet said.

55
00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:33.596
"He's a good mechanic, isn't he?

56
00:02:34.576 --> 00:02:37.599
In any case, I went to check the float this morning.

57
00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:42.362
The taillight was fixed, but a whole case of candy was missing!"

58
00:02:42.382 --> 00:02:45.525
"Candy?" Jackson looked confused.

59
00:02:45.545 --> 00:02:48.127
"Yes." Mrs.

60
00:02:48.187 --> 00:02:49.188
Sweet leaned forward.

61
00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.982
"I was going to use it to decorate my float," she whispered.

62
00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:57.143
Henry covered his mouth to hide his smile.

63
00:02:58.104 --> 00:03:01.945
Mrs. Sweet was whispering, acting as if everything was top secret.

64
00:03:02.786 --> 00:03:05.687
But she decorated her float with candy every single year!

65
00:03:05.707 --> 00:03:10.829
"There have been some problems with raccoons around town lately," Jackson said.

66
00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:13.130
"Or perhaps a stray dog."

67
00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.691
"I don't think it was an animal."

68
00:03:15.891 --> 00:03:17.352
Mrs. Sweet said, frowning.

69
00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.041
"The shed door wasn't locked, but it was shut tightly.

70
00:03:21.921 --> 00:03:24.162
The latch can only be opened by a person."

71
00:03:24.182 --> 00:03:25.722
"I see."

72
00:03:26.422 --> 00:03:29.743
Jackson jotted a few notes, and then tucked his notebook away.

73
00:03:29.763 --> 00:03:32.704
"Well, give me a call if you think of anything else."

74
00:03:36.085 --> 00:03:38.446
Henry and Maggie followed the reporter outside.

75
00:03:38.466 --> 00:03:40.886
"Is that it?"

76
00:03:41.266 --> 00:03:41.967
Maggie asked.

77
00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.387
"Aren't you going to examine the crime scene?"

78
00:03:45.268 --> 00:03:46.468
Jackson looked surprised.

79
00:03:47.136 --> 00:03:49.177
"That's a job for the police, not for me."

80
00:03:49.197 --> 00:03:53.818
"But we thought you'd want to get to the bottom of the story," Henry said.

81
00:03:53.838 --> 00:03:56.439
"Why don't you go interview Mr.

82
00:03:56.479 --> 00:03:58.640
Newman?" Jackson shrugged.

83
00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.200
"I suppose I could.

84
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.581
The auto repair shop is on my way back to the office."

85
00:04:06.922 --> 00:04:09.103
Soon the three of them were at Newman's Auto Shop.

86
00:04:10.163 --> 00:04:11.244
Henry had known Mr.

87
00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:12.204
Newman all his life.

88
00:04:13.184 --> 00:04:18.207
Henry's parents said the people of Belltown were lucky to have such an honest and hardworking mechanic in

89
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.828
town. Mr.

90
00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.849
Newman listened to why Jackson was there.

91
00:04:21.869 --> 00:04:24.090
"What do you want to know?"

92
00:04:24.651 --> 00:04:26.452
he asked in his usual gruff way.

93
00:04:26.472 --> 00:04:28.973
"Did you stop by to fix Mrs.

94
00:04:29.013 --> 00:04:30.214
Sweet's taillight last night?"

95
00:04:30.414 --> 00:04:31.314
Jackson asked.

96
00:04:32.235 --> 00:04:33.175
Mr. Newman nodded.

97
00:04:33.195 --> 00:04:35.597
"Fixed the light and then went home."

98
00:04:35.617 --> 00:04:38.618
"Did you see a case of candy near the float?"

99
00:04:38.898 --> 00:04:39.679
Maggie asked.

100
00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:41.260
"Didn't notice.

101
00:04:41.952 --> 00:04:44.474
I was there to fix the light, not to sightsee."

102
00:04:45.315 --> 00:04:46.636
Mr. Newman checked his watch.

103
00:04:46.656 --> 00:04:48.597
"Is there anything else?

104
00:04:49.077 --> 00:04:49.938
I have work to do."

105
00:04:50.899 --> 00:04:51.959
"No, there's nothing else.

106
00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.361
Thanks for your time," Jackson said.

107
00:04:54.381 --> 00:04:57.704
"Wait," Maggie said as Jackson turned to leave.

108
00:04:57.724 --> 00:05:01.306
"Mr. Newman, are you making a float for the parade?"

109
00:05:02.207 --> 00:05:03.648
Mr. Newman looked surprised.

110
00:05:03.668 --> 00:05:05.049
"Of course not.

111
00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:07.611
I don't have time for that sort of silliness."

112
00:05:08.331 --> 00:05:09.052
He hurried off.

113
00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:12.053
"Sorry, kids," Jackson said.

114
00:05:12.073 --> 00:05:14.353
"It looks like there's no mystery here."

115
00:05:14.373 --> 00:05:16.654
"What about the missing candy?"

116
00:05:16.874 --> 00:05:17.614
Maggie asked.

117
00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.395
"And that threat?"

118
00:05:19.655 --> 00:05:20.355
Henry added.

119
00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:22.816
"Threat? What threat?"

120
00:05:22.976 --> 00:05:23.856
Jackson asked.

121
00:05:24.836 --> 00:05:28.497
Henry realized they'd never told the reporter about the comment on the website.

122
00:05:29.117 --> 00:05:30.498
He quickly filled Jackson in.

123
00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:34.359
Jackson pulled out his smartphone and opened the website.

124
00:05:34.379 --> 00:05:36.899
"I don't see any threatening comments."

125
00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.480
"I'll show you."

126
00:05:39.212 --> 00:05:41.555
Henry took the phone and scrolled through the comments.

127
00:05:42.496 --> 00:05:43.357
The ones from Mrs.

128
00:05:43.397 --> 00:05:46.421
Sweet and Miss Bishop were there, along with several others.

129
00:05:47.322 --> 00:05:48.964
But the threatening comment was gone!
